.IX Title "Lucy::Search::SortSpec 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Search::SortSpec 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Search::SortSpec \- Specify a custom sort order for search results.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 10
\&    my $sort_spec = Lucy::Search::SortSpec\->new(
\&        rules => [
\&            Lucy::Search::SortRule\->new( field => \*(Aqdate\*(Aq ),
\&            Lucy::Search::SortRule\->new( type  => \*(Aqdoc_id\*(Aq ),
\&        ],
\&    );
\&    my $hits = $searcher\->hits(
\&        query     => $query,
\&        sort_spec => $sort_spec,
\&    );
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
By default, searches return results in order of relevance; SortSpec allows
you to indicate an alternate order via an array of
SortRules.
.PP
Fields you wish to sort against must be \f(CW\*(C`sortable\*(C'\fR.
.PP
For a stable sort (important when paging through results), add a
sort-by-doc rule as the last SortRule.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 1
\&    my $sort_spec = Lucy::Search::SortSpec\->new( rules => \e@rules );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new SortSpec.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBrules\fR \- An array of SortRules.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Search::SortSpec isa Clownfish::Obj.
